From 71316b6dc13a2fc765477a9ef305cbdd322909ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:28:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: memory space of the fields, libraries kept
 loaded with TBB

The libraries of behaviours, models and material properties export the
memory space in which the fields must be located
(<f>_generic_parallel_memory_space): `host` (computations on the host),
`device` (computations on a device which can't access the ordinary memory
of the host) or `any` (fields copied if needed). It is set when the
library is compiled (MFront/GenericParallel/MemorySpace.hxx), since the
target of some programming models is selected by the compiler (C++ parallel
algorithms and OpenMP with nvc++, unified memory mode) or by the
configuration of a library (execution space of Kokkos, data transfers of
SYCL). The calling code can thus check the location of its data without
knowing the backends.

The configurations linking TBB mark the libraries as never unloaded
(-Wl,-z,nodelete): unloading TBB while its threads are alive crashes the
process, for instance when the libraries loaded by a calling code are
closed at the end of the process.

The tests check the exported memory space.
